          "category": "performance",
          "severity": "high",
          "line": 3652,
          "description": "streaming NIM responses are buffered whole: the body is ReadAll'd (up to 128MB) and only then copied to the client, so a stream's first byte waits for the whole generation. pipe lastResp.Body for isStream and tee the usage tail only",
          "addedAt": "2026-10-16T00:51:01.754Z"
        },
        {
          "category": "performance",
          "severity": "medium",
          "line": 43,
          "description": "upstreamBodyLimit 128MB x up to 16 in-flight slots = ~2GB peak, and debug mode keeps a second copy (respBodyBuf); the comment calls it a bound against memory exhaustion",
          "addedAt": "2026-10-16T00:51:01.785Z"
        },
        {
          "category": "improvement",
          "severity": "low",
          "line": 365,
          "description": "lastKey/ModelLock stop inserting at 4096 distinct model ids and never evict, so stickiness and per-key model lockouts silently stop applying to new ids",
